    {
      "entry_id": "metric.movement-timing.definition",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "metric_definition",
      "topics": [
        "movement_timing",
        "kinematics_thresholds"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "decel_frac high",
        "decel_frac low",
        "peak_position low",
        "peak_position high"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:movement_time_ms",
        "metric:time_to_peak_ms",
        "metric:acceleration_duration_ms",
        "metric:deceleration_duration_ms",
        "metric:decel_frac",
        "metric:peak_position_pct"
      ],
      "text": "movement timing 描述一次 flick 从开始、加速、到达峰值、减速到稳定的时间结构。decel_frac 是减速时长占主运动时长的比例；peak position 和 time-to-peak 描述峰值出现位置。它们应结合具体事件、任务需求和可比历史理解。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "product:analysis-contract:movement-timing",
          "source_level": "product_contract"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "deterministic_rule",
      "limitations": [
        "未校准时不得把单次数值标为健康或异常。",
        "时间结构不能单独证明动作策略或身体原因。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [],
      "supported_uses": [
        "definition",
        "diagnostic_scope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "kinematics.movement-timing.mechanism",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "kinematic_mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "movement_timing"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "decel_frac high",
        "decel_frac low",
        "peak_position low",
        "peak_position high"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:time_to_peak_ms",
        "metric:decel_frac",
        "metric:peak_position_pct"
      ],
      "text": "点对点运动通常包含前馈主运动与受任务精度约束的末端调整。更早或更晚的峰值只说明本次时间分配不同；是否更有效必须同时看准确性、停止成本和同任务历史。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "research:woodworth-1899:two-component-movement",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        },
        {
          "source_ref": "research:becker-2020:aiming-kinematics",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "research_supported",
      "limitations": [
        "手臂 reaching 的机制不能直接提供短时鼠标 flick 的绝对阈值。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [
        "不同任务、目标宽度和输入设置会改变速度曲线。"
      ],
      "supported_uses": [
        "mechanism",
        "research_context"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "metric.braking-linearity.definition",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "metric_definition",
      "topics": [
        "braking_linearity",
        "min_jerk_vs_uniform_decel"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "linearity high"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:linearity"
      ],
      "text": "减速线性度描述速度下降过程相对连续制动模型的偏离程度。它和 SPARC 是不同构造：linearity 关注制动形态，SPARC 关注速度谱平滑度。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "product:metric:braking-linearity",
          "source_level": "product_contract"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "deterministic_rule",
      "limitations": [
        "不能把 linearity 单独解释为手抖、张力或肌肉状态。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [],
      "supported_uses": [
        "definition",
        "diagnostic_scope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "kinematics.braking-linearity.mechanism",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "kinematic_mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "braking_linearity",
        "min_jerk_vs_uniform_decel"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "linearity high"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:linearity"
      ],
      "text": "minimum-jerk 轨迹和平稳的恒定减速不是同一个理想模型。linearity 只能回答速度下降是否接近当前定义的制动形态，不能代替 jerk 或频域平滑度。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "research:flash-hogan-1985:minimum-jerk",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        },
        {
          "source_ref": "doc:aim-kinematics-research:6.1",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "research_supported",
      "limitations": [
        "当前产品 linearity 定义与外部研究模型的对应关系必须随 metric version 解释。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [
        "一条轨迹可以较平滑但不接近恒定减速，也可以接近线性却含局部波动。"
      ],
      "supported_uses": [
        "mechanism",
        "research_context"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "metric.sparc.definition",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "metric_definition",
      "topics": [
        "smoothness_sparc",
        "sparc"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "sparc low"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:sparc"
      ],
      "text": "SPARC（Spectral Arc Length）是基于速度幅度谱形状的平滑度指标。产品中只应在相同 metric version、相近任务与质量条件下解释本次分布或个体历史变化；数值本身不提供身体原因。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "product:metric:sparc",
          "source_level": "product_contract"
        },
        {
          "source_ref": "research:balasubramanian-2012:sparc",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "deterministic_rule",
      "limitations": [
        "未校准时不得使用绝对健康阈值。",
        "不能从 SPARC 直接推断握持、肌肉张力或疼痛。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [],
      "supported_uses": [
        "definition",
        "diagnostic_scope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "limitation.sparc.external-validity",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "limitation_counterevidence",
      "topics": [
        "smoothness_sparc",
        "sparc"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "sparc low"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:sparc"
      ],
      "text": "SPARC 的部分可靠性证据来自时长更长的 reaching 或康复任务。健康玩家短时鼠标 flick、不同 polling rate 和重采样条件下的绝对可比性仍需产品数据验证。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "research:cornec-2024:sparc-duration-bias",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        },
        {
          "source_ref": "doc:coach-prescription-manual:1.6",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "research_supported",
      "limitations": [
        "不能把外部研究中的 ICC、CoV 或阈值直接迁移为本产品健康线。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [
        "极短信号可能降低频域估计稳定性；任务时长和预处理会影响解释。"
      ],
      "supported_uses": [
        "diagnostic_scope",
        "research_context"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "metric.stopping-corrections.definition",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "metric_definition",
      "topics": [
        "stopping_corrections",
        "reverse_ratio_trap"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "reverse_ratio high"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:settle_time_ms",
        "metric:corrective_count",
        "metric:reverse_ratio"
      ],
      "text": "settle time、corrective count 与 reverse ratio 分别描述主运动后稳定所需时间、后续修正次数和反向运动比例。它们可以定位停止阶段成本，但不能单独确定导致修正的策略、设置或身体原因。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "product:analysis-contract:stopping-corrections",
          "source_level": "product_contract"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "deterministic_rule",
      "limitations": [
        "必须结合事件质量、运动时长和任务精度。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [],
      "supported_uses": [
        "definition",
        "diagnostic_scope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "limitation.reverse-duration-bias",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "limitation_counterevidence",
      "topics": [
        "stopping_corrections",
        "reverse_ratio_trap"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "reverse_ratio high"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:reverse_ratio",
        "metric:corrective_count",
        "metric:settle_time_ms"
      ],
      "text": "修正次数和反向运动会受运动时长、采样质量与分段规则影响。解释 reverse ratio 时应同时查看 settle time、corrective events 和相同 metric version，避免把较长动作自动判为控制更差。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "doc:coach-prescription-manual:1.4",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "research_supported",
      "limitations": [
        "离散事件计数必须保留 segmentation version。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [
        "较长任务天然提供更多出现修正的机会。"
      ],
      "supported_uses": [
        "diagnostic_scope",
        "research_context"
      ]
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "kinematics.submovements.mechanism",
      "entry_version": 1,
      "status": "active",
      "category": "kinematic_mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "submovements",
        "submovement",
        "submovement_types"
      ],
      "signals": [
        "submovement two-stage"
      ],
      "metric_refs": [
        "metric:submovement_count",
        "metric:submovement_overlap",
        "metric:corrective_count"
      ],
      "text": "submovement 将 initial movement 与后续 corrective movement 描述为可重叠或可分离的运动成分。较低 overlap 可以描述更分离的两段式结构，但不能脱离准确性和任务需求自动判定好坏。",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_ref": "research:woodworth-1899:submovement",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        },
        {
          "source_ref": "research:meyer-1988:optimized-submovements",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        },
        {
          "source_ref": "research:novak-2002:overlapping-submovements",
          "source_level": "academic_peer_reviewed"
        }
      ],
      "max_claim_level": "research_supported",
      "limitations": [
        "当前短时 flick 的 Type 1/2/3 可靠分类尚未完成。"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [
        "终止型 submovement 与误差修正型 submovement 可能具有不同意义。"
      ],
      "supported_uses": [
        "definition",
        "mechanism",
        "diagnostic_scope"
      ]
    },
    {
